@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# smallpt — The light playground
+
+Kevin Beason’s original C++ smallpt path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Open `index.html` through any static web host. All path tracing runs locally in a module Web Worker; no rendering service or cross-origin isolation is needed.
+
+The checked-in `public/smallpt.js` and `public/smallpt.wasm` are ready to serve. `npm run build` rebuilds them (requires `emcc` on PATH). `npm test` exercises the actual WebAssembly module in Node without starting a server.
+
+The page automatically renders the Cornell box. Randomize colors rerenders with new colors for both interior spheres and the side walls. Color pickers, quality, and resolution changes also rerender. Render again uses a fresh path seed; reset restores the original palette and default settings. The download button exports the current canvas as PNG. Controls can restart an in-progress render.
+
+## Implementation and attribution
+
+- `src/smallpt-original.cpp`: unmodified upstream source from https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/smallpt.cpp, by Kevin Beason (2008).
+- `src/smallpt-wasm.cpp`: browser adapter using the original ray intersections and radiance integrator. Replaces the CLI/PPM output with progressive 2×2 subpixel sampling, an RGBA buffer, and scene color exports.
+- `public/render-worker.js`: loads WASM, schedules row batches, publishes progressive frames, and cancels stale jobs.
+- `public/reference.png`: upstream's 25,000-sample output, displayed only while the first live frame loads, labeled as a reference render. Retrieved from the original smallpt distribution.
+- `src/LICENSE.txt`: original MIT license. No external images or generated artwork are used.
+
+The original command-line main is renamed during compilation, preserving upstream source. Compiler warning compatibility flags accommodate its 2008 initialization syntax. The Emscripten output is compiled with `-O3`, without OpenMP, filesystem support, or a server component.
